."No flying teapots exist" is a weaker claim than"There are no flying teapo=
ts", since there might be flying teapots in the domain of discourse, but no=
ne in the extension of "exists".  As to what to do about "nothing", there i=
s the useful bit in Alice, cited in CLL, to show the problems of taking "no=
thing" to be the name of something. On the other hand, there is Fridegesis =
(sp?) who noted it must be the name of a very big something, since God made=
 the world out of nothing, and look how big it is!
